    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7f58cab5-9641-5b48-a636-9574a131ae52",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $E$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 1 \\\\ -11 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -11 \\\\ -6 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
