      ":question/id": "10061234-92e4-5bbb-99eb-4fe758ed4740",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 11 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 0 \\\\ -10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
